course: dictionary
lesson: 11506
title: Agriculture and farming words
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Agriculture is a long, formal word for farming. It means growing crops and keeping animals for food, wool and other products. Once you know it, you can spot it in geography and history texts.
explain: «Modern agriculture uses machines to plant and harvest crops.» The clues are modern, machines, plant and harvest. So agriculture means the work of farming, not just the farm building or the animals on their own.
explain: Look at the word parts. Agricultural is the adjective, so «agricultural land» is land used for farming, and «an agricultural show» is a show about farming. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: does «farming» still make sense? If yes, you have it.
fact: Agriculture means farming: growing crops and keeping animals.
fact: Agriculture is also the science and business of farming.
fact: The adjective is agricultural, as in «agricultural land», which is land used for farming.
fact: Early people began agriculture when they stopped wandering and started growing wheat and keeping animals.
fact: Because of agriculture, people could stay in one place, so villages and towns could grow.
exercise: «Farmers in the valley use agriculture to grow wheat and keep sheep.» What does agriculture mean here? | A kind of cloud that brings rain | A type of rock found in hills | A shop that sells garden tools | *Farming: growing crops and keeping animals
exercise: «The agricultural show had prize cows and huge tractors.» Find and copy the word that is about farming. | prize | *agricultural | tractors | show
exercise: Why did villages and towns grow after agriculture began? | The wind carried houses to new places | People built more roads for fast cars | *People could stay in one place and grow their own food | Animals stopped needing grass to eat
test: «Modern agriculture uses machines to plant crops.» What is modern agriculture? | *Farming that uses modern machines | A school where children learn to swim | A shop that sells bicycles | A museum of old farm tools
test: Ben's family grow wheat on their agricultural land. What is agricultural land? | Land where only trees are allowed to grow | *Land used for farming | Land covered in houses and shops | Land at the bottom of the sea
exam: Which sentence uses agriculture correctly? | Agriculture is the name of a famous footballer | *Agriculture helped early people settle in one place | Agriculture is a colour used in paintings | Agriculture is a loud noise made by the sky
